========================================================================
PLAIN ENGLISH (RULES 1.10)
========================================================================

**What changed**
RFC-002 used to say the swarm created `Process.Args` and `FS.Walk`.
Those modules are not in the tree. The RFC now says they were **not**
shipped. The named-gap is still open.

**Why it matters**
A closed RFC that names missing modules is pride (SINS #3). Agents
would try to import floors that do not exist.

**What is not done**
No args parser. No directory walk. No refuse stubs this turn (not
needed for a doc restatement). RFC-003 still repeats the old claim
(F19). String regex/templating still overclaimed until F35 closes.
No push.

