========================================================================
FINDING F32 (CRIT) — closed by honesty
========================================================================

Severity: CRIT (doc false-success on named-gap floor)
Assumption destroyed: RFC-002 §Resolution "Created a `Process.Args` module."
Surface: `openOODA/RFC-002-StdLib_Completion.oot`; product `ooda/std/**`
Would smoke catch?: no — no smoke is wired to a missing module.
Residual after fix?: **named-gap still open.** No `Process.Args`. Future
owner may land `args_parse` or a ≤20-line refuse stub. This pass: restate.

Repro (shell, dual independent):

```
# run 1 2026-08-12T20:08:21Z
# run 2 2026-08-12T20:08:55Z
grep -rln "args_parse\|fn process_args\|Process\.Args\|fn parse_args" ooda/std
# (no matches) exit=1 both runs
test -f ooda/std/args.oo; echo $?   # 1
test -f ooda/std/core/args.oo; echo $?  # 1
test -f ooda/std/os/args.oo; echo $?    # 1
test -f std/src/args.oo; echo $?        # 1
```

False-friends (not a parser): `ooda/std/os/process.oo` is spawn/wait/kill/
exec + syscall residual. No CLI flag / env struct ingest.

